[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-1b8359f5-f2ec-478f-b0f9-e3078a35b3ae\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Thu 16 Apr 2026 16:15 - 16:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-oceania-ix\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Oceania IX</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">AI for Software Engineering 19</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/fabiopalomba1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Fabio Palomba</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"1b8359f5-f2ec-478f-b0f9-e3078a35b3ae\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Inside Out: Uncovering How Comment Internalization Steers LLMs for Better or Worse</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Virtual Attendance\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Virtual Attendance\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/5a83481a-76b0-4d52-a281-ed633e8995d2/small?1776349051000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>While comments are non-functional elements of source code, Large Language Models (LLM) frequently rely on them to perform Software Engineering (SE) tasks. Yet, where in the model this reliance resides, and how it affects performance, remains poorly understood. We present the first concept-level interpretability study of LLMs in SE, analyzing three tasks - code completion, translation, and refinement - through the lens of internal comment representation. Using Concept Activation Vectors (CAV), we show that LLMs not only internalize comments as distinct latent concepts but also differentiate between subtypes such as Javadocs, inline, and multiline comments. By systematically activating and deactivating these concepts in the LLMs\u2019 embedding space, we observed significant, model-specific, and task-dependent shifts in performance ranging from -90% to +67%. Finally, we conducted a controlled experiment using the same set of code inputs, prompting LLMs to perform 10 distinct SE tasks while measuring the activation of the comment concept within their latent representations. We found that code summarization consistently triggered the strongest activation of comment concepts, whereas code completion elicited the weakest sensitivity. These results open a new direction for building SE tools and models that reason about and manipulate internal concept representations rather than relying solely on surface-level input.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.16790\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/aaronimani\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Aaron Imani\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/aaronimani/6f198b75-7c0e-463c-86f6-8b0f6073cfce/micro-avatar?1783975620000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Aaron Imani<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/mohammadmoshirpour\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Mohammad Moshirpour<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/iftekharahmed\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Iftekhar Ahmed\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/iftekharahmed/f17a082d-ec89-4490-8969-bf5ef0585fc5/micro-avatar?1783972714000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Iftekhar Ahmed<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California at Irvine</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br><div class=\"row\" style=\"padding:4px 0px;\"><label class=\"col-sm-2 control-label\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Pre-recorded Presentation</label><div class=\"col-sm-10\"><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-8\"><div class=\"embed-container\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"//www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/VHl-DzJizxw?enablejsapi=1\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen ></iframe></div></div></div></div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\">pauseOnCloseModal(\"modal-1b8359f5-f2ec-478f-b0f9-e3078a35b3ae\")</script></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/248/Inside-Out-Uncovering-How-Comment-Internalization-Steers-LLMs-for-Better-or-Worse\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-1b8359f5-f2ec-478f-b0f9-e3078a35b3ae').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
